From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Serialization: don't call getAPValue() on a value-dependent TypeTraitExpr

TypeTraitExpr::getAPValue() asserts !isValueDependent(), but
ASTStmtWriter::VisitTypeTraitExpr() calls it unconditionally for any
non-boolean type trait, including value-dependent ones (e.g. a
dependent use of __builtin_structured_binding_size). In an
assertions-enabled build this aborts while writing a BMI; in a
release build it happens to be well-defined only because
TypeTraitExpr::Create(..., APValue) always allocates the trailing
APValue slot, so an empty APValue is read back -- but that's
incidental, not intentional.

Port the guard already present on `main` (as of the IsComparisonResult
work) back onto the 23.1.0 writer: write an empty APValue for the
value-dependent case instead of dereferencing the (absent) stored one.

Local repro:

    export module repro;
    export template <class T>
      requires(__builtin_structured_binding_size(T) >= 0U)
    inline constexpr int v = __builtin_structured_binding_size(T);

    clang++ -std=c++23 --precompile repro.cppm -o repro.pcm

aborts on an assertions build of 23.1.0 without this patch.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of
the llvm-project monorepo (i.e. no leading `clang/` component), to
match this repo's clang derivation's sourceRoot (clang-src-.../clang)
and its other patches (e.g. purity.patch's "lib/Driver/...").
---
 lib/Serialization/ASTWriterStmt.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterStmt.cpp b/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterStmt.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterStmt.cpp
+++ b/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterStmt.cpp
@@ -2250,6 +2250,8 @@ void ASTStmtWriter::VisitTypeTraitExpr(TypeTraitExpr *E) {
 
   if (E->TypeTraitExprBits.IsBooleanTypeTrait)
     Record.push_back(E->TypeTraitExprBits.Value);
+  else if (E->isValueDependent())
+    Record.AddAPValue(APValue());
   else
     Record.AddAPValue(E->getAPValue());
 
